  "launch_notes": "1B dense-equivalent: ~1.2B active params/token (attention 4*h^2=16.8M + top-2 of 16 experts @ 16.8M each per layer, 24 layers), 6.9B total. Expert count 16 and EP=16 give 1 expert/GPU; TP=1 keeps all-to-all disjoint from attention TP; cap factor 1.25 = capacity = tokens*topk*1.25/16, balances load-balance loss vs padding overhead; min capacity 4. Use --moe-token-dispatcher-type alltoall (flex/DeepEP if available) for top-2, --moe-router-load-balancing-type aux_loss with coeff 1e-2, --moe-grouped-gemm, --moe-permute-fusion. On 32x H100 80GB: ~38GB/GPU peak fits in 80GB (params/grads/Opt states ~14GB + checkpointed activations ~10GB + comm buffers); ~1.0M tok/s aggregate (~31k/GPU) at ~35% MFU; expect roughly 3x slower on A100-80GB. Launch: torchrun --nnodes=4 --nproc_per_node=8 pretrain_gpt.py --tensor-model-parallel-size 1 --pipeline-model-parallel-size 1 --num-layers 24 --hidden-size 2048 --num-attention-heads 32 --seq-length 2048 --max-position-embeddings 2048 --vocab-size 32768 --num-experts 16 --moe-expert-parallel-size 16 --topk 2 --moe-train-capacity-factor 1.25 --moe-eval-capacity-factor 1.25 --moe-min-capacity 4 --moe-loss-coeff 0.01 --swiglu --micro-batch-size 8 --global-batch-size 512 --bf16 --use-flash-attn --optimizer adam --lr 3e-4 --min-lr 3e-5 --lr-decay-style cosine --weight-decay 0.1 --clip-grad 1.0 --split 98,2,0 --data-path /data/dataset --deepspeed --deepspeed_config ds_config.json, where ds_config.json sets train_batch_size=512, train_micro_batch_size_per_gpu=8, gradient_accumulation_steps=32, fp16/bf16 auto, zero_optimization stage 1."
